=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,000
Did you ever think

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,360
I might choose the red ticket?

15
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:42,280
My first instinct at that moment

16
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,120
was the blue ticket.

17
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:45,340
(Nods)

18
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,800
I did consider your feelings

19
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,520
and

20
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,760
the way you think and your pace.

21
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:52,480
So don't overthink it.

22
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:53,160
And don't feel

23
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,840
any pressure or anything.

24
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,600
Just be yourself.

25
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:00,240
Back then,

26
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,560
I hesitated a little.

27
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:03,880
Because of what happened with Xing.

28
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:09,560
Actually, I didn't want

29
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,440
to bring up another thing

30
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,120
that could affect your emotions.

31
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,840
I understand.

32
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,000
After all, she's family.

33
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,600
Your attention

34
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,960
would naturally be on this.

35
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,200
I thought about it for a while.

36
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,680
If you didn't choose the red ticket,

37
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:25,840
I might

38
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:27,400
not know what you were thinking.

39
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,840
Because neither
of us really expressed it.

40
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,280
Then I started wondering if

41
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,080
I was the only one thinking so much.

42
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:39,660
(Fidgets)

43
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,080
What about now?

44
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,120
Things have changed.

45
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,320
Because you chose the red ticket.

46
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:48,820
(Smiles)

47
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,680
So how do you think

48
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,040
your red and blue ratio is?

49
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,760
Forty-sixty.

50
00:01:58,240 --> 00:01:59,020
You don't say anything.

51
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:00,520
You don't say anything either.

52
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,240
I just feel like

53
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,840
I wasn't as proactive

54
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,440
before.

55
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,199
Honestly, that day I really wanted

56
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:09,639
to throw the Jasmine Coin.

57
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,479
But...

58
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:13,200
you came back
with your hands in your pockets.

59
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:14,920
Yeah.

60
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,440
That really touched me.

61
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:17,240
Yeah.

62
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:19,000
I'm really lacking

63
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,920
in this kind of practical expression.

64
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,080
Did you ever think

65
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,080
about choosing C?

66
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,120
If you weren't here?

67
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,700
I might have considered C.

68
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,580
(Would consider choosing C without you)

69
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,020
(Couples House)

70
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,640
The ocean!

71
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:49,200
Look, there's blue light over there.

72
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,040
Yeah.

73
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,600
It's so beautiful.

74
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,520
(Hugs)
Blue light.

75
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,720
Incredible.

76
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,360
Absolutely incredible.

77
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:02,800
This is amazing.

78
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,180
Oh my gosh.

79
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:06,160
This really is

80
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,960
a trip I'll never forget

81
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,560
for the rest of my life.

82
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,200
Guys, should we

83
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,240
