84
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,560
Let's go take a look.

85
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,680
How do we get in?

86
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,520
Pull it over like this.

87
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:24,630
Wow.

88
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:25,730
Wow!

89
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,320
It connects.

90
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:28,880
They're connected.

91
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,440
Rooms 901 and 902 are connected.

92
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,440
One, two, three, four, five, six.

93
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,280
There are six rooms.

94
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,400
There's another room over there.

95
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,040
Upstairs.

96
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,200
Six rooms?

97
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,360
This counts as two.

98
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,320
So there are also single rooms.

99
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,960
Are we not staying in the same space?

100
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,080
No way.

101
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,880
But these are the only ones
we can see at a glance.

102
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,520
These are two single beds.

103
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:52,620
Wow.

104
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,600
This room...

105
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,760
This room is pretty nice.

106
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:55,520
I love it.

107
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,000
There's more upstairs.

108
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,560
Those two rooms are connected.

109
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,280
The upstairs rooms.

110
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:05,200
The view here is so open.

111
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,640
I think this room is nice.

112
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,440
When you open the curtains, you can see

113
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,400
the view opposite.

114
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:11,640
Oh my gosh.

115
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,080
This room really

116
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:13,800
reminds me

117
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,440
of my original

118
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,360
Green Space.

119
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:19,720
This room...

120
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:22,360
It has better privacy.

121
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,280
There's another room here.

122
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,880
That one is a single room, right?

123
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:26,600
Yeah.

124
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,920
This room's pretty nice too.

125
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:30,960
It's actually quite spacious.

126
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,920
Looks like the food is ready over there.

127
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,160
The food's here?

128
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,480
The food's here.

129
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:36,520
Have a seat.

130
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,560
Sit, Sha Yue'er.

131
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,480
Sit.

132
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,640
Take your seats.

133
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,640
Let's eat.

134
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:50,840
I'll get you some food.

135
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:51,360
Okay.

136
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,560
Is there anything you want?

137
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,280
Anything's fine. You choose.

138
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,360
Get whatever you want to eat.

139
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,200
I'll grab some side dishes.

140
00:04:59,120 --> 00:04:59,800
What's this?

141
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,600
Scallops. Take one.

142
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,240
Okay.

143
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,160
I'll go over there.

144
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:11,760
What's this?

145
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,680
Is this potato?

146
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,880
No, it looks like fruit.

147
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:16,520
Yeah, mango.

148
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,920
Grilled mango.

149
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,480
Yeah.

150
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:20,560
I'll get some mushrooms too.

151
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:25,600
A little bit.

152
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,120
We don't really know this one either.

153
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:30,360
Okay.

154
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:30,960
I can't tell what it is.

155
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:31,400
Okay.

156
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,780
(Places in front)

157
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,040
That light over there is so bright.

158
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,480
Can we walk down there

159
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,680
to the shore?

160
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,920
We should be able
to walk along the coastline.

161
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,040
It looks so beautiful.

162
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,120
It'd probably look
even better during the day.

163
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,760
Early morning or at sunset.

164
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,160
But my

165
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,480
presentation is waiting for me too.

166
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,080
I can sit there

167
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,120
and work on my presentation.

168
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,640
You can finish it when we get back.

169
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,520
I'll take a look later.

170
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:19,720
This egg

171
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,160
looks pretty good.

172
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,160
I'll get you a spoonful.

173
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,000
Okay.

174
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,800
Thanks.

175
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,960
When should we go for a walk?

176
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,480
Wake up early to see the ocean.

177
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,880
We can

178
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:32,280
set a time.

179
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,520
Let's all go for a walk
by the beach together.

180
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,400
Whoever doesn't get up,
we'll go wake them up in their room.

181
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,120
Watch the sunrise tomorrow.

182
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,800
Let's see who's missing.

183
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,260
(Teases)

184
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,160
Then I'll sleep in the sea.

185
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,080
Can we watch the sunrise
the day after tomorrow?

186
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,720
Tomorrow let's just sleep
until we naturally wake up.

187
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,060
I won't allow myself
to wake up that late.

188
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:50,460
(Jokes)

189
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,160
You won't sleep tomorrow?

190
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:54,720
Of course I will.

191
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,400
I was just joking.

192
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,440
I don't know what it is.

193
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,560
You can use this

194
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,680
to try a little bit of this

195
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,480
mystery food.

196
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,460
(Glances)

197
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,120
Here.

198
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,040
(Serves x1)
Thanks.

199
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:19,280
(Serves x2)
Here.

200
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,120
Thanks.

201
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:20,480
Here.

202
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,160
(Serves x3)
I've got some. Eat.

203
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,800
I've got some. I ate already.

204
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,600
(Serves)
Thanks.

205
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:26,440
I'll peel it for you.

206
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,100
(Takes it)

207
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:31,680
This one's still pretty intact.

208
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:35,840
(Hands over)
This is really fresh.

209
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,400
What else do you want to eat?

210
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,120
Which one do you want?

211
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:46,560
No...

212
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,040
I'm almost done.

213
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,280
Is there anything you can't reach?

214
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,440
I think I've tried everything.

215
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,400
What else do you want?

216
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,160
I've tried everything too.

217
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:54,760
Do you play ping pong?

218
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:56,720
Can you play ping pong?

219
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,240
I think

220
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,360
you won't be my opponent.

221
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,960
I'll let you use both hands.

222
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,240
Let's play something.

223
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:08,800
How about this?

224
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,880
The loser can't use their hands.

225
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:11,520
They have to crawl from here to there.

226
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,520
No hands.

227
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,680
No hands?

228
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,160
Crawl over without using your hands?

229
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,200
Isn't that just walking?

230
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,160
Crawling means crawling.

231
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,000
But you can't use your hands.

232
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:21,720
Like this.

233
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,520
Just wiggle forward.

234
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,360
Yeah, wiggle.

235
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:24,720
You go.

236
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,240
No hands.

237
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,080
Fight me with your feet.

238
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,280
Crawl. I said the loser crawls.

239
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:27,960
You just want to wiggle.

240
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,920
Just say it directly.

241
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:32,640
You want to wiggle?

242
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,799
Then just wiggle.

243
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:34,760
Why do you have to make me

244
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,640
play ping pong with both hands?

245
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,200
Just wiggle if you want to.

246
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:39,559
I believe you're good.

247
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,280
But if you let me use both hands, I...

248
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:41,919
I'm actually really good.

249
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:42,919
I catch everything.

250
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:43,520
No more letting you win.

251
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,240
Let's play normally.

252
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,640
Then we're not playing.

253
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,760
Then later,

254
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,480
should we choose our rooms or...

255
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,120
Sure.

256
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,240
We can choose our rooms first.

257
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,560
Then unpack.

258
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,600
Rock paper scissors.

259
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,320
Or we can do it
the old way and draw lots.

260
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,240
Yeah. This side is one and two.

261
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,200
The middle is three and four.

262
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,000
The single room on the far side is five.

263
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,360
Whatever number you draw is your room.

264
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,120
Okay.

265
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:04,400
You go first.

266
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,600
Come on, Cao Yiheng.

267
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,000
I got one.

268
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,120
What number is this?

269
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,120
What number is this?

270
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:17,800
Is it two?

271
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,320
Two.

272
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,200
Yu Yang,

273
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:20,940
we're in the same room.

274
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:21,760
We're in the same room?

275
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:22,160
Okay.

276
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:23,480
I got five.

277
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:23,960
You got five.

278
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,680
I got five.

279
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,960
So I'm in the single room, right?

280
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,040
Yeah, you're in the single room.

281
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,000
Three.

282
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,080
You're four, right?

283
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,680
I got four.

284
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:32,360
We're in the same room.

285
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,280
The middle one?

286
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,200
Yeah, the middle.

287
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,280
Okay, that's fine.

288
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,960
How are we going to arrange rooms?

289
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:39,160
The single room
and double room are connected.

290
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,680
So it's basically a three-person room.

291
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,120
That one is actually
a three-person room.

