Do you remember that scene?

588
00:19:05,250 --> 00:19:06,600
The stargazing room.

589
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,000
Then pointing at the stars like this.

590
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:09,720
Like this.

591
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:10,640
Yeah.

592
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,120
Really.

593
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,880
You can see so much here.

594
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:23,800
Seashells.

595
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:26,840
Let's pick up seashells.

596
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,120
What's wrong?

597
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:37,040
Nothing. I was just looking at the sea.

598
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:38,280
I zoned out a little.

599
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,960
It doesn't feel real.

600
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:40,680
(Doesn't feel real)

601
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,200
This moment right now.

602
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:42,800
This scene.

603
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:43,440
This moment.

604
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:44,960
It's so beautiful.

605
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:45,760
Yeah.

606
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,040
It really is.

607
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,480
And this trip was so spontaneous.

608
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:53,400
(Spontaneous trip)
It really was a last-minute trip.

609
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,600
You might only get a moment
like this once or twice in life.

610
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,240
To just leave whenever you want.

611
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,380
(Places seashell)

612
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,960
Let's make a wish.

613
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:09,760
Okay, don't say it out loud.

614
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,080
So I'll make a wish on the seashell

615
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:14,040
and throw it away?

616
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:17,200
Make a wish on the seashell.

617
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,080
I'll give you two big ones.

618
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:18,880
Thanks.

619
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,780
(Glances)

620
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:36,320
This wish is really long.

621
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:37,000
Let's go.

622
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:39,560
Throw it.

623
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:42,300
(Getting up together)

624
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,280
Run!

625
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,920
Now the waves will carry it away.

626
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:06,840
Let's go back.

627
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,720
Let me think of an activity.

628
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:13,600
Arm wrestling.

629
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,080
Arm wrestle.

630
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,640
I'll be the referee.

631
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:16,880
Come on.

632
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,040
Come on.

633
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,720
Go easy on me.

634
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,680
Don't break my arm.

635
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,160
I'm weak.

636
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:21,560
I'm not that strong.

637
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:22,680
Come on.

638
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,160
Arm wrestling?

639
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,280
Seriously?

640
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:26,600
Three.

641
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:27,800
Wait.

642
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:28,520
Move this away.

643
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:28,960
Three.

644
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:30,440
Two.

645
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:31,000
One.

646
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:34,960
Elbow.

647
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,840
I'll lose first.

648
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:37,840
He's holding back.

649
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:38,800
Totally holding back.

650
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:39,800
I can't watch this.

651
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:43,080
Such a gentleman.

652
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,200
You're drinking mine, aren't you?

653
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:47,680
I don't know.

654
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:49,360
This definitely isn't yours.

655
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:51,480
I grabbed the wrong one.

656
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,160
Sorry.

657
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,080
I'm really sorry.

658
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:54,360
Wipe it off.

659
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,520
Let's fix it.

660
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:01,140
(Glances)

661
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,920
But I feel like you two

662
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:02,840
are becoming more and more alike.

663
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:03,920
Yeah.

664
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,200
You really do look alike.

665
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,440
You two just blend together so well.

666
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,560
Like you have

667
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,160
a bit of each other.

668
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,640
Even your smiles feel the same.

669
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:13,760
Maybe it's because we
look at each other so much.

670
00:22:15,980 --> 00:22:16,940
(Glances)

671
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:24,800
Maybe looks change because of thoughts.

672
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:25,800
If you keep thinking about someone,

673
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:26,560
you'll slowly

674
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,680
become more like them.

675
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:28,600
I think so too.

676
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,800
When two people
are together for a long time,

677
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,480
they slowly become like each other.

678
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:33,000
Then in a few days, Yu Yang

679
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:34,560
will have huge eyes.

680
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:36,200
I'll just...

681
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,560
I'll just become like this
in the future.

682
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,280
Like this.

683
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:43,920
You already look handsome.

684
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,000
Your eyes are already big enough.

685
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:52,160
Have you ever thought about

686
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:53,600
what superpower you'd want

687
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:54,920
if you had one?

688
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,320
That's a great topic.

689
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,400
For superpowers,

690
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,120
do you mean based on

691
00:22:58,120 --> 00:22:59,040
the Twelve Talismans

692
00:22:59,040 --> 00:22:59,840
from Jackie Chan Adventures?

693
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,120
Any power you want.

694
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:02,760
If it's my choice,
I'd definitely want to fly.

695
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,000
You want to fly?

696
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,440
What would you do after flying up?

697
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,520
If I could fly,

698
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,120
I'd just land somewhere.

699
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:09,640
I'd want time stop or teleportation.

700
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,960
So what you mean is,

701
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:11,360
you can go somewhere else instantly?

702
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,040
Yeah, teleportation.

703
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:12,960
Exactly, teleportation.

704
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,600
For example,
I could teleport into the sky,

705
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,360
but I wouldn't stay floating there.

706
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:18,080
I'd fall after teleporting up.

707
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:19,240
Before I hit the ground,

708
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,360
I'd have to choose
another place to teleport to.

709
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:21,320
So basically,

710
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:22,560
you don't actually
have the ability to fly.

711
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:23,800
You just change your position...

712
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:25,080
I instantly move

713
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,680
to another place.

714
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,000
I want

715
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,520
time

716
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:32,080
reversal.

717
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,480
Time reversal?

718
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,720
Being able to control time.

719
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:35,640
Do you think

720
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,000
after using that power,

721
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,360
when you return to a certain point,

722
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:39,520
would it create

723
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:40,320
a new timeline?

724
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:41,760
Or would it stay
on the original timeline?

725
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,800
In theory,

726
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,760
it would create a new timeline.

727
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:47,720
Changing time would be amazing.

728
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,000
Going back to the past.

729
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,240
That's actually
a really interesting question.

730
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:50,760
I saw a clip

731
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:51,400
online today.

732
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:51,800
They

733
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,440
asked,

734
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:54,240
would you be willing

735
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,080
to go back,

736
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,480
say,

737
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,440
twenty years ago?

738
00:23:58,440 --> 00:24:00,120
If you had that ability,

739
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:02,080
but everything you've experienced

740
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,160
would have to happen all over again,

741
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,200
would you go back?

742
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:04,760
Definitely not.

743
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:06,080
I definitely wouldn't.

744
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:07,520
If it was only the first part, I would.

745
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:08,560
But if it includes the second part,

746
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:09,040
having to experience everything again,

747
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:09,520
I wouldn't either.

748
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:10,840
Twenty years ago,
there were many things,

749
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:12,520
including your precious memories.

750
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:13,480
Some good, some bad.

751
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,160
Wouldn't you feel like

752
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,560
you were just watching a movie?

753
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,080
Like seeing my life from my perspective?

754
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,160
A third-person perspective.

755
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,240
Would you?

756
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:22,160
I would.

757
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,360
You could only watch.

758
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:24,960
You couldn't change anything
or make decisions.

759
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:25,640
Right.

760
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:26,800
Every stage of life,

761
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:28,080
I'd want to experience it again.

762
00:24:29,120 --> 00:24:30,960
I think life is about experiences.

763
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:31,920
If there are things

764
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:32,720
I could experience again,

765
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:34,440
that would be pretty interesting.

766
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:37,240
We're here.

767
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:37,880
We're on the island.

768
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:38,720
We're here.

769
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:41,640
Can we buy coconuts here?

770
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:46,920
Hello.

771
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:50,640
Can we buy coconuts?

772
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:53,040
How many coconuts would you like?

773
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:53,720
How many do we need?

774
00:24:54,320 --> 00:24:54,920
Do you all drink them?

775
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,320
Sure.

776
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:57,200
Then one for each person?

777
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:57,720
Thank you.

778
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:58,360
Four.

779
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:00,000
Should we get one more for Sha Yue'er?

780
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,040
Five. Thank you.

781
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:04,240
Would you like ice?

782
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,440
It can't go in here, right?

783
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,320
But you can use a cup.

784
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:07,240
They'll give you an iced cup.

785
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:08,120
Okay.

786
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:11,240
So would you like an iced cup or...

787
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:12,840
Just give me one iced cup.

788
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,240
Okay, I'll bring it over for you.

789
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:18,200
Thank you.

790
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:20,240
I finally know

791
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:21,040
how to say thank you.

792
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:23,440
Thank you.

793
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:25,360
We've paid. Let's go.

794
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:26,160
Thanks, Liang Xiaoyu.

795
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:26,880
Thank you.

796
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:28,320
It's okay.

797
00:25:28,380 --> 00:25:30,420
(Don't go anywhere. The next episode
is even more romantic.)
